>I need to run a shell script that will check to see if a process is
>running, and if it is not, then make run it.

	This is usually done by having the process you want to check write
its process-id to a file someplace. The second process just sits in a loop
and wakes up every minute (or whatever) and does a "kill 0" on the process
you want to check. You then test the exit value of kill. Easy.

#!/bin/sh
while true; do
	sleep 60
	kill -0 `cat /some/dir/process.pid`
	if [ $? -ne 0 ]; then
		echo "process died"
		/start/some/process
	fi
done

mjr.

PS - (another option is to not run those LPMuds that crash alla time, if
that was your question. ;) )
