Your assumption is, I believe, correct. The DUV-11 is a 
synchronous interface. I believe the top speed is on the order of 
9.6Kb or so (I would have to dig out my old peripherals handbook 
to confirm). Unfortunately, it does not have DMA, only (as I 
recall) a two character silo. Using such devices on MicroVAXes 
has often been problemmatic, the interrupt servicing demands of 
even a medium speed line running synchronously are quite 
impressive.
 
I hope that the above is helpful, 
 
