Ray,

 One recommendation I would make is to ask your supplier about a DEC version
of firmware for the disk. I'm pretty sure that folks like Clearpoint, Maxtor,
Micropolis, Seagate and Hitachi have such a thing (some of them maintain a
PROM for each of the major system vendors). This can make your life a lot less
complicated. 

 Please be careful of drives that can only run Synchronous through a jumper
setting. The console firmware on the DECstations will run the drive in asynch
and the SCSI driver will bring it up synchronous. A drive which is hard wired
will not generally work (the SCSI spec requires the ability to NEGOTIATE for
synchronous...a hard jumper doesn't exactly fit that description).

  Just some thoughts that I hope you'll find helpful. Enjoy your PDS5000/25, I
think you'll like it.

				Thanx,
				  AJ


