Unfortunately, it's a bad design for a networked window system. It's a GREAT
design for a research system, where you want the application to have minute
control over the display. Over a network, though, there's just too much
traffic. Intuition (the Amiga window system) like NeWS puts more of the
responsibility in the hands of the server (Intuition *does* use a message
passing protocol to manage the display, even though it's all shared memory).
I'd really really like to see a better compromise. 8 1/2 looks good.
