Good question, Sergio, and one that does NOT have a self-evident answer.
The line-editing characters in VMS are, I believe, hardcoded into the terminal
driver, and there is no obvious way to remap ^H to do what <DEL> does.

It has been hypothesised that the TFF utility (Terminal Fallback Facility)
would let you achieve what you want, but as far as I know, no one has ever
done this.

As a VMS bigot, I'm sorry ...

