I would guess that most application writers do not use NeWS and opt for X since
it would increase the target market and make the code more portable.  Of course
this has tradeoffs such as not allowing it to take as much advantage of graphic
co-processors, etc.

>If this were true then why does my SparcStation 1 run SimCity 3 times *slower*
>than my Amiga 2000 did?!?!?!?!!!  Yet, that same SS1 is able to drive both

Probably becase your Amiga 2000 has graphics co-processors to do most of the
work, plus it typically has less resolution.  (1152x900x256 vs 640x400x32? -
typically - thats a lot of stuff to move) Also, all frame buffers for the
Sun are not created equal.  There are accellerated frame buffers (such as
the GX) but these do not speed things up as much since X is operating with
more basic objects.  In the same system an application that could pass more
complicated objects for the frame buffer to create (instead of the processor)
could run significantly faster. 

