  Well, I just looked up in my sources for a vt330 emulator and there
is no way to set the answerback string from the host side. You can
however request the answerback message from the host (^E). You can
also program UDK's from the host, but you can't request them to be 
"typed" like the answerback string. I suspect they may have had you 
in mind when they didn't implement that feature :-)

