In article <1992Oct19.162900.20843@oct17.dfe.dec.com> e_alsberg@csc32.enet.dec.com (Ed Alsberg) writes:

>DECmate II and III's have a few missions in life.  The main thing they do
>is run a dedicated WPS-8 word processor package.
>WPS also includes a terminal emulator, so you can pretend to be a VT100.
>The DECmate II had an optional hard drive, hence the larger package than the
>DM III.
AMong other things. A DECmate II has room for 1 or 2 sets of floppy
drives and a hard drive if you only want one floppy drive "set". There
are three "slots" which can hold (from right to left) the APU (Z80
card), XPU ( 8088 ?) for DOS 2.1, and a graphics card. I have a II
with an APU, & a (whopping) 5meg hard drive and the only XPU's I had
I've since given away to a more "worthy" user (Charles Lasner, who is
really the BEST source for Decmate info I've found.... you can find
him over in alt.folklore.computers, where this discussion really
belongs (Or alt.sys.pdp8 - Did anyone mention that the Decmates all
use a single chip version of the PDP-8 for their CPU. 
>I'm not certain about the DM III, but the DMII had options such as CP/M
>coprocessor, Math coprocessor, and I _think_ a DOS emulator of some type.

I still support some Decmate III+ users here (down to 5 at last count)
so I have a III+ sitting next to a spare VT1200 in my office. From
what I've been told (If i'm wrong it's because of my memory, not my
source) the III can only have a hard drive up to 20 megs while a II
can handle anything up to 84meg if you can figure out how to format
it. Also, the II has floppy drive "sets" which are two SS drives while
the III+ has a single DS drive that emulates the drives on a II.

>WPS-8 itself is a fairly nice wordprocessor, IMO.  I have a DMII at home,
The most recent incarnation is WPS-Plus... using WPS on a Decmate &
using All-in-1 are very simular in "feel." If you can use WPS on a
Decmate you can use All-in-1..... it just does more.

>The monitor, I think, is the VR201, the same as used on the Rainbow and

>PRO series, along with an LK201 kb.  Ideally, you want an LK201 which has 
>WPS-8 key markings.  
My home Decmate doesn't have a WPS keyboard but sometime I'm going to
get around to taking the stickers I have at work & put them on it....

It'll use almost any DEC keyboard.... (Not sure about that but the
III+ I have is using something that looks like it came from a
VT1000....


I can't claim to be the final source of info on these things.... just
a fan of obsolete equipment...

