Date: Tue, 20 Oct 1992 17:47:51 GMT
Lines: 17

>[...] I'm not sure if your article supports my hypothesis that W/NT is a
>development from VMS or whether it supports the hypothesis that W/NT is
>a totally new rewrite.

	NT is not even a rewrite. It's by the same guy who did the core of
VMS and RSX, but it's a whole new operating system. You have to assume that
whatever the original VMS looked like, it probably bore as much resemblance
to VMS5.X as V7 UNIX does to OSF/1. Things change fast, hard, and ugly, when
they get turned into a major product.

	There are some glimmerings of VMS-isms in NT. There are a lot of
things that clearly aren't VMS-isms (log based file systems, and so on).
There are a few little nods to VMS, but you're making a mistake if you
cubbyhole it as a "UNIX alike" or "VMS rewrite" or anything silly like
that.

mjr.


