I don't know yet, but DEC has put alot of effort into cross-compilers and 
image translators in the past couple of years.  What I understand is that
they are rewriting them to have "replaceable" front and backends (not really,
but they will probably have a collection for cross-compilation).
Don't be surprised to see DEC marketing their compilers for a variety of
platforms, and options for cross-compiling for non-DEC target platforms.

One of the interesting integrations for the new OpenVMS Fortran compiler
it the ability to specify the floating-point memory format at compile time
or at run-time. A routine that everyone has written at one point in time,
but someone finally put in as a useful extention to Fortran.
