> something, that, in a case where it is fed some bad postscript, will spit
> out a page saying what the error is.
> 
> Thanks in advance,
> 
> Anthony
-- 
Anthony,
 
There are a variety of error handlers for PostScript devices. 
Most spoolers/symbionts include an error handler as part of their 
standard printer setups. Offhand, I would not vouch for the side 
effects of attempting to load one's own error handler on top of 
the symbiont's own handler. I am sending you (by e-mail) a copy 
of the error handler I use. 
 
In a more general case, you should, for security reasons, not be 
able to load any code outside of the SERVER loop. Most error 
handlers will attempt to load themselves outside of the server 
loop. 
 
I hope that the above is helpful. If I can be of further 
assistance, please feel free to contact me via e-mail.
 
