DECmate II and III's have a few missions in life.  The main thing they do
is run a dedicated WPS-8 word processor package.
WPS also includes a terminal emulator, so you can pretend to be a VT100.
The DECmate II had an optional hard drive, hence the larger package than the
DM III.
I'm not certain about the DM III, but the DMII had options such as CP/M
coprocessor, Math coprocessor, and I _think_ a DOS emulator of some type.

WPS-8 itself is a fairly nice wordprocessor, IMO.  I have a DMII at home,
but mainly use it for dialup to work.  My wife occasionaly plucks out
a document in WPS-8.

The monitor, I think, is the VR201, the same as used on the Rainbow and
PRO series, along with an LK201 kb.  Ideally, you want an LK201 which has 
WPS-8 key markings.  


