|
|Could those of you running DECnet on Sun post or email comments on the 
|product you are currently using?  Ease of use, configuration,
|reliability, bugs, etc.  Whatever you think we should know.
|If there are sufficient responces and interest, I will summarize.

Our company, ki research inc, supplies DECnet, LAT and MOP on Sun as well
as most other workstations including Ultrix.

Our DECnet implements Endnode, Level 1, and Level 2 routing node types.
Email between Unix and VMS is supported and configured automatically at
install time.  X<->DECwindow support is included.  Incoming and outgoing
NCP NICE protocol is supported [the DECnet configuration protocol].

Our command set is modeled after the VMS commands though we do support
the DECnet/Ultrix and SunLink command line interfaces.  We support most
of the DECnet/Ultrix program library.

Our DECnet file transfer software has an option for storing VMS file
attributes to allow files to be restored to a VAX in the correct VMS
file storage format.  Typically, files stored on UNIX lose most of the
VMS file storage information such as fixed record length and record
attributes.

Our LAT supports incoming and outgoing login, incoming user defined
services, incoming and outgoing LAT printing.  Outgoing login supports
connecting to password protected services.

All our protocol stacks have a user application interface allowing
users to write their own applications.

Send email to sales@ki.com for more info or call us at 1-800-945-4454
or direct at 410-290-0355.

