> My DS5000/200 was recently upgraded from CX/VR-262 to HX/VRT-19. While
> I like the increased real estate and color and graphics performance, I
> find the screen is less sharp than I expected. In particular, it is
> also less sharp than the VR-262, at least when the VR-262 was focused
> properly. (My experience with the VR-262 was that the focus drifted
> and had to be adjusted periodically.)

  I believe the VR262 is a mono monitor. The VRT19, being a color monitor,
will always be less sharp than a mono unit. Also, if you use the "small
font" option for things like DECterm, the dots are only a single pixel wide,
so they will appear fuzzy on the screen, depending on whether or not they
land on a stripe or slightly off.

  There's always the possibility that you got a bad monitor... I'm quite
happy with my VRT19.

