cks@hawkwind.utcs.toronto.edu (Chris Siebenmann) writes:

>We're trying to move an HX graphics card (said PMAGB-BA HX 8-plane
>colour card) from a 5000/240 where it was temporarily installed to a
>5000/200 that is its real home, and, well, it isn't working. The
>5000/200 doesn't recognize it as a console device, and neither does
>Ultrix (more or less: kernel configuration messages vanish into thin
>air, but everything else talks to the serial terminal). The card still
>works fine in the 5000/240, and the rest of the hardware is identical.

The HX does work on a 5000/200.

What ROM version do you have on the 5000/200?  It should be at least
5.3c.  ( to find out what version of the ROMs you're running, type "cnfg 7"
at the boot prompt ).

What is the value of the "console" boot environment variable?  It should be
set to "*" ( to do this, type "setenv console *" at the boot prompt).

What version of ULTRIX are you running?  The HX requires ULTRIX 4.2A or later.

You might also have to run doconfig to configure your kernel and devices if
you have not previously used a basic framebuffer (like the CX or MX) on your
5000/200.

