I think part of the "number of external SCSI devices on a
DECstation 5900" restriction comes from the fact that the
system was designed to have all the SCSI disks in the
storage expansion drawers.  If you can't fit the device
in one of these, then you have to run it outside the
box which uses up lots of cable.

On the DECsystem 5500, the length of cable needed to get
outside the box is probably not as much.  You'll still
have to watch the cable and length, but you should have
more leeway on the 5500.

