	While it's feasible to run LAT over Token Ring, Digital currently
has no implementation that supports it.

	We are persuing this issue for future releases of VMS and Unix-based
operating systems and adapters for such.   In the sort term, a Translating
Ethernet to Token Ring Bridge would be your only path to a host system.
The Ethernet packets need to be mapped to 802.2 SNAP packets on the Token
Ring and 3 multicast addresses need to be mapped into Functional Addresses.
This can be done with Proteon p4100+ and CNX Bridging Routers in R12.0

	The only thing stopping the PATHWORKS PCs is a check for If Token Ring,
then print a "not supported" message.  A clever PC hacker can no-op that
out of LAT.EXE, it will work.  (using PW for DOS V4.1A ... the "A" is
important")

