*Greetings from the DFWLUG*

The DFWLUG is celebrating our 10th anniversary October 10th at 
White Rock Lake in Dallas.  As we celebrate 10 years of DECUS 
in North Texas the LUG has undergone many changes.  Members 
come and go, speakers come and go, and the computer industry 
changes but one thing has stayed the same our unopposed chairman
Stuart Renes.

Stuart is stepping downs from the reins of leadership after 10 years 
but his time with us has left us much in his debt and much changed
as DFWLUG has grown since 1982.

Stuart has stepping down in the same month as Ken Olsen but we still 
hope to use his experience, dedication and expertise as the grand 
emeritus and founder of the DFWLUG.  Old DECUS folks never really 
retire, they simply change jobs for a couple years and come back again.

Our sincere thanks and all our best Stuart, we'll miss your leadership 
but will enjoy your support as the most extra-ordinary DFWLUG member 
ever.

The picnic is going to be a legendary celebration for a legendary LUG 
chairman.  

The DFWLUG is very excited about our NEXT 10 years of DECUS and our
group's technical excellence too, but before we travel that great 
adventure we're going to celebrate our LAST 10 years in style.

BBQ, Awards, Music will start off the festivities. DFWLUG limited edition 
coffee mugs, posters, balloon animals and family fun will provide the zip
to make this a picnic to remember. 

Digital has graciously donated a 19" Color VXT2000 Xwindow terminal, 
an Infoserver, and PCs as prizes for a special DFWLUG raffle to be held 
at the picnic. (Sorry, only current DFWLUG members will be allowed to 
participate in the raffle.)

With a picnic on Saturday and our regular DFWLUG meeting on Tuesday
night we are going to get a double dose of DECUS this month -- But 
it's only once every 10 years!

See you at the picnic!

*The DFWLUG Staff*  

