 Digital - Hudson semiconductor manufacturing facility registered to
	international quality standards
	{Livewire, Worldwide News, 25-Sep-92}
   Digital has announced that its Hudson, Mass. semiconductor manufacturing 
 facility has been registered by the Quality Management Institute (QMI) to 
 International Organization for Standardization (ISO) standard 9002.  
   Hudson is one of two Digital sites manufacturing the recently announced
 Alpha AXP family of semiconductors.
   The ISO 9000 series of international quality assurance standards is becoming
 a prerequisite for conducting business in Europe and other parts of the world.
 Registration of a quality program requires adherence to strict guidelines and 
 comprehensive auditing by a qualified external agency such as QMI. With
 Hudson's registration, all four of Digital's semiconductor facilities 
 worldwide are now registered to ISO 9002. As of Quality System Update's last 
 publication (Summer, 1992), fewer than 400 quality systems in all industries 
 are registered in the U.S.
   In a ceremony at the Hudson facility, a QMI representative presented Digital
 with a plaque signifying the Hudson site's accomplishment.
   Ed Caldwell, vice president, Semiconductor Operations, remarked, "We are 
 pleased with this recognition of our ongoing commitment to quality. With the
 European Economic Community's adoption of ISO 9000 standards, this
 certification becomes much more significant in the global marketplace."  

