In article <1992Sep30.150119.9940@cs.cornell.edu>, chapman@cs.cornell.edu (Richard Chapman) writes:
> 1) What is the pinout of the connectors to the 4 ports on a DLV11-J
> (4 SLU's) Q-bus card? There is currently a ribbon cable with a male DB-9
> connector at the other end in each port connector on the card, but the
> DB-9 does not appear to use the "modern" rs-232 pin assignment. Can anyone
> tell me the pin assignment? 

Well, I don't know the full pinout, but a bit of meter work on a KA630 
distribution panel (which I'm pretty sure is the same) reveals:

Looking down into the 10-way sockets on the board:

        1         9
         . g . t .
         . r   . .
        2         10

(g = Ground, r = Receive, t = Transmit)

A quick squiz at the tracks on a real DLV11-J tends to confirm this
arrangement.

As to the DB9: Basically, translate the DB25 pinout pin for pin, at least 
for the data lines (the signal lines differ slightly, mainly due to the 
fact there's no pin 20 on a DB9!), ie 2=Tx, 3=Rx, 7=Gnd.  From (possibly 
faulty) memory, RTS, CTS, DSR & DCD are where you expect them to be, ie pins 
4, 5, 6 & 8 respectively, and pin 9 is DTR.  I'm not sure about pin 1; I 
thought it was RI, but the KA630 panel insert has it strapped to the 
chassis.

