A BA23 has a 230W PSU, which is a fairly mondo sort of power supply 
compared to your average PC.  The BA123 is even bigger.  

I've got two disk drives running in my BA23, of the elderly power-hungry
variety.  The power budget is knocking against the limit, but repacing
drives with more modern ones would pull things down quite nicely.

The BA123 has a _lot_ of space for drive mounting, but it is assumed that
some of those drives will be either floppies or tapes and not suck a lot
of power all the time.  Again, putting in more modern drives helps -- an
RD54 pulls a _lot_ less juice than an RD52 for example.  

